/-!
# Facet primes and normalized monomial valuations of complete toric models

Source: the auxiliary algebraic input recorded in the DAG for the complete models of
ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé VI 1.4 and 1.6(i)--(ii), printed pp. 69--70; ILO
motivates the models and does not state this theorem. The proof is agent-formulated:
derive the rational cone facets, identify their boundary ideals, and use the
monomial-ratio uniformizers in the prime localizations. The degenerate monoid and
parameter-free cases are included.

(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-facet-valuations)
-/
@[expose] public section
universe u v w
namespace ToricMonoid

/-- Facet primes and normalized monomial valuations: for a sharp fs monoid `P` and a
normal domain `R` that is a complete model `B_k(P,n)` or `B_C(P,n)/(θ)` with chart
monomials `z`, `R` is Noetherian, every `z q` is nonzero, the facets of `σ` are finitely
many with unique primitive normals `ν_F` cutting out `σ`, the ideals `p_F` are the
distinct height-one primes containing a chart monomial, `R_{p_F}` is a DVR, and its
normalized valuation sends `z^q` to `ν_F(q)`; for `P = 0` everything is empty.
Source: auxiliary input to ILO VI 1.4 and 1.6(i)--(ii), printed pp. 69--70; Stacks
00FN, 0316, 00PD, 00KQ for the commutative-algebra steps
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-facet-valuations).

Proof (the node's 18 steps):
1. `lem-trf-sharp-cone-lattice-intersection`: `G` finite free, `σ` generated by finitely
   many `a_j ∈ P`, pointed and spanning, `P = σ ∩ G`. If `G = 0`, no facets.
2. `lem-trf-rational-cone-dual-finite`: `σ` is cut out by a finite irredundant family of
   nonzero forms `h_i`; `x₀ = ∑ a_j` satisfies all of them strictly.
3. Irredundancy gives `f_i` with `h_i(f_i) = 0`, `h_j(f_i) > 0` for `j ≠ i`; perturbing
   along a basis of `ker h_i` shows `F_i = σ ∩ ker h_i` spans `ker h_i`: distinct facets.
4. Every facet `F = σ ∩ ker h` is some `F_i` (an interior-perturbation contradiction),
   so the `F_i` are exactly the facets and cut out `σ`.
5. Clearing denominators and dividing by the gcd gives the primitive `ν_F`; uniqueness
   since two primitive forms with one kernel differ by `c ∈ ℚ_{>0}` with `cℤ = ℤ`.
   Scaling `f_i` into `G` gives `f_F ∈ P ∩ F` with `ν_H(f_F) > 0` for `H ≠ F`.
6. The coefficient ring is Noetherian; `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian`,
   `lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-noetherian`, `lem-weil-pbc-surjective-image-noetherian`
   make `R` Noetherian.
7. `lem-trf-sharp-monoid-positive-grading` and `lem-trf-monoid-completion-coefficients`
   identify `B_L(P,n)` with all coefficient families on `P × ℕⁿ`; `z^q ≠ 0` in case (i).
8. In case (ii) `θ` has constant coefficient `p`; weight induction shows `z^q ∉ (θ)`.
9. `S = P ∩ F` is a sharp fs face of `P`.
10. Truncation to exponents in `S` is a surjection `B_L(P,n) → B_L(S,n)` with kernel
    generated by the `z^q`, `q ∉ F`.
11. `R/p_F ≅ B_k(S,n)` or `B_C(S,n)/(θ_S)`, a nonzero normal domain by
    `lem-trf-log-regular-saturation-normality`; so `p_F` is prime and `z^q ∈ p_F` iff
    `q ∉ F`.
12. `z^{f_F} ∈ p_H \ p_F` gives distinctness; `p_F ≠ 0`; `A_F = R_{p_F}` is a
    Noetherian local domain.
13. With `ν_F(e) = 1` and `N` large, `π = z^{e+Nf}/z^{Nf}` is a nonzero element of the
    maximal ideal.
14. For `q ∈ P`, `z^q = u_q π^{ν_F(q)}` with `u_q` a unit; hence `p_F A_F = (π)`.
15. By `def-sc-discrete-valuation-ring` (Stacks 00PD (4)) `A_F` is a DVR;
    `lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-local-dimension-le-generators` and prime correspondence give
    height one.
16. `lem-sc-dvr-valuation-ring-characterization`, `lem-sc-dvr-valuation-arithmetic`:
    `v_F(π) = 1`, units have value `0`, so `v_F(z^q) = ν_F(q)`.
17. A height-one prime containing a monomial contains some `p_F` (else a monomial
    `z^b` outside it has a power divisible by `z^a`), hence equals it.
18. For `P = 0`: no facets, `z^0 = 1` lies in no prime, `V = 0`; `n = 0` changes no step. -/
theorem complete_toric_facet_valuations
    (P : Type u) [AddCommMonoid P]
    (hfs : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFineSaturatedMonoid (Multiplicative P))
    (hsharp : ∀ q : P,
      IsUnit (Multiplicative.ofAdd q) → q = 0)
    (n : ℕ) (R : Type w) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R]
    (z : P → R) (hmodel : IsCompleteModel.{u, v, w} P n R z) :
    IsNoetherianRing R ∧ (∀ q : P, z q ≠ 0) ∧
      Set.Finite {F : Set (RationalSpace P) | IsFacet P F} ∧
      ∃ (ν : Facet P → Lattice P →+ ℤ)
        (h : Facet P → RationalSpace P →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ),
        (∀ F : Facet P, IsPrimitiveNormal F (ν F) ∧
          (∀ μ : Lattice P →+ ℤ, IsPrimitiveNormal F μ → μ = ν F) ∧
          IsRationalExtension (ν F) (h F) ∧
          F.val = {v | v ∈ cone P ∧ h F v = 0}) ∧
        (cone P : Set (RationalSpace P)) = {v | ∀ F : Facet P, 0 ≤ h F v} ∧
        Function.Injective (boundaryIdeal z) ∧
        (∀ F : Facet P,
          (boundaryIdeal z F).IsPrime ∧ boundaryIdeal z F ≠ ⊥ ∧
            ∀ Q : Ideal R, Q.IsPrime → Q < boundaryIdeal z F → Q = ⊥) ∧
        (∀ Q : Ideal R,
          (Q.IsPrime ∧ Q ≠ ⊥ ∧ (∀ J : Ideal R, J.IsPrime → J < Q → J = ⊥) ∧
            ∃ q : P, z q ∈ Q) ↔ ∃ F : Facet P, Q = boundaryIdeal z F) ∧
        (∀ (F : Facet P) [hp : (boundaryIdeal z F).IsPrime],
          IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime (boundaryIdeal z F)) ∧
            ∀ [hdvr : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime (boundaryIdeal z F))]
              (q : P),
              -WithZero.log
                ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.maximalIdeal
                  (Localization.AtPrime (boundaryIdeal z F))).valuation (FractionRing R)
                    (algebraMap R (FractionRing R) (z q))) = ν F (latticePoint q)) ∧
        (Subsingleton P → IsEmpty (Facet P) ∧ Subsingleton (RationalSpace P) ∧
          Set.range (boundaryIdeal z) = ∅ ∧
          (cone P : Set (RationalSpace P)) = Set.univ) := by
  sorry
end ToricMonoid
